---

#dash.flags
  Most urgent first: Festgefahren (werkrevisor escalated, RED for an hour
  without a new commit, ERROR, or a run without verdict), Nacharbeit (conflict
  or red build on the user's own pull request), Dein Approval (a foreign pull
  request without werkrevisor or with a final YELLOW or ORANGE), Mergen (the
  user's own pull request approved by another human), Wartet auf Review (the
  user's own pull request waits for another human), Von dir approved.
  Only the chips are coloured, not the row.

#dash.pwa
  User request of 2026-10-10: the Werkregie frontend becomes a progressive
  web app, installable on phone and desktop.

  The service worker caches the page, styles, fonts and icons only. The API
  answers carry private data behind the access token and are never cached by
  the service worker; offline the page shows the last state it holds, marked
  with its age. The local mode on localhost counts as a
  secure context, so the PWA works there too.

#dash.matrix
  User request of 2026-10-10: messages that matter to the user show in
  Werkregie, read-only. Werkregie signs in with the user's own account as a
  device of its own, because many rooms are end-to-end encrypted and only a
  device of the account can read them. It runs in the relay, so the device
  keys stay on the user's machine.

  The homeserver is configured; there is no default, and no real homeserver
  appears in the repository. Shown: every direct message, mentions in every
  room (found after decryption, since the server cannot see them in encrypted
  rooms), and all messages of the configured rooms. The server gets only room,
  sender, time and the start of the text.

  Reading Element Desktop's own store was dropped: it has no interface, and
  its data lies encrypted in IndexedDB.

#dash.matrix.link
  Element Desktop opens element:// links (io.element.desktop:// for the
  stable app when a nightly build holds element://); on a phone matrix.to
  opens Element. Which form, configurable or chosen by the device, is open.

#dash.notify
  Werkregie posts what a pull request asks of whom into a Matrix room, for
  colleagues too. A separate feature, later. A bot account of its own will
  do; which events go to whom is open.

#ops.github
  GitHub carries main only. Until Werkator does it, main is pushed by hand
  with git push github.

#ops.port
  The server runs on port 18091, picked because it was free; Hostsharing has
  not confirmed it for the booked service yet.
